{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nPrivate reconciler forwarding bindings retain a second owner after the ADR-0111 private-shim policy landed on main. On the current implementation base, the old private bindings in this leaf are:\n\n- `apply_inbound_records._inbound_update_write_edit_event`, which only forwards to the canonical event writer in `apply_inbound_events`.\n- `reconcile.py` module-level compatibility bindings for helpers now owned by `pass_support`, `reconcile_helpers`, or `runtime`: `StatusMappingError`, `preflight_status_mapping`, `_commit_binding_store_snapshot`, `_read_local_tickets`, `SelectionStaleError`, `ensure_selection_current`, `narrow_selection_inputs`, `_build_filter_target_set`, `_mutation_matches_filter`, `_build_plan_entries`, `_NoOpSyncLogger`, `_write_prev_snapshot_key_set`, `_accepts_synced_fields_out`, `_accepts_client`, `_accepts_ticket_plans`, `_advance_baselines`, `_advance_peer_parent`, `_write_facade_enabled`, `_resolve_pass_transport`, `bind_operation_runtime`, and `compose_reconciler_runtime`.\n- `Mode.rank()`, which remains only because the comparison dunders call it.\n\nThese are private internal names, so ADR 0111 requires exactly one canonical binding and atomic migration of source, test, string, dynamic import, and monkeypatch consumers.\n\n## Seam decision\n\n`reconcile.<name>` monkeypatch targets are internal compatibility shims under ADR 0111, not a public/operator/wire/data contract. This story will remove that seam and migrate consumers to the canonical owner (`pass_support`, `reconcile_helpers`, `runtime`, or a phase function that remains owned by `reconcile.py`).\n\nLive-DC guardrail: `tests/external/test_reconcile_live.py` is marked `external`, is excluded from default Verified (`-m \"not integration and not external\"`), and skips unless live Jira credentials plus `acli` are present. It does not monkeypatch `reconcile.<name>`; it only documents/asserts the preview plan shape that mirrors `_build_plan_entries`. Therefore removing the private `reconcile._build_plan_entries` attribute does not break a live-DC load-bearing seam. The test will be updated to cite the canonical plan-entry owner/contract while preserving the live non-destructive preview oracle.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. Recensus the current base with semantic reference lookup plus raw string scans for imports, `getattr`, dynamic-load, and monkeypatch target strings for each old private name.\n2. Add or strengthen held-out RED oracle coverage under the authorized test surface proving the old shim surfaces are gone while observable behavior remains: inbound update writes still persist edits through `apply_inbound_events`, the reconcile spine still observes monkeypatches installed on canonical helper/runtime owners or on phase functions still owned by `reconcile.py`, live preview remains non-destructive/well-formed, and `Mode` ordering keeps its current order without `rank`.\n3. Migrate every in-scope source/test/string/dynamic/monkeypatch consumer to the canonical owner before deleting the old bindings.\n4. For `reconcile.py`, do not merely delete passive re-exports. Rewrite the in-module call sites in `_load_snapshots`, `_save_and_commit_bindings`, `_persist_and_log`, and `reconcile_once` so they resolve the canonical owner at call time where the collaborator moved, while preserving the remaining `reconcile.py`-owned phase seams (`_load`, `_load_snapshots`, `_persist_and_log`) that are not compatibility re-exports.\n5. Rewrite `Mode` comparison dunders to compare against the existing ordering data directly, then remove `Mode.rank()`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- inbound event-write compatibility re-export in `apply_inbound_records.py`\n- canonical inbound writer in `apply_inbound_events.py`\n- reconciler pass-helper/runtime bindings and their call sites in `reconcile.py`\n- canonical helper/runtime owners in `reconcile_helpers.py`\n- `Mode.rank()` and comparison callers in `mode.py`\n- tests under `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler`\n- `tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_baseline_normalization.py`\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_reconciler_apply_bindings.py`\n- `tests/external/test_reconcile_live.py`\n\n## Testing\n\n- Held-out RED/GREEN oracle in the authorized test surface for canonical owner behavior, absence of old shim bindings, and mode ordering without `rank`.\n- Mutation teeth: temporarily reintroduce one removed shim/bare-name alias/rank path and confirm the held-out oracle returns RED, then restore.\n- Raw scans over the approved file impact for old private names, `getattr`, dynamic import strings, and monkeypatch strings.\n- Focused reconciler unit/integration/interface/external collection tests covering inbound, orchestration/reconcile spine, live preview shape, and mode ordering; then `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the ticket verify command set.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every old in-scope core/reconciler private name has no production, test, string, dynamic-load, or monkeypatch consumer through the old owner.\n- [ ] The canonical owner is the only binding for each migrated operation in the authorized implementation paths.\n- [ ] `reconcile.py` helper/runtime call sites are repointed to canonical owners at call time, and tests prove canonical-owner monkeypatches are observed by the running code path where the collaborator moved.\n- [ ] The live-DC external preview harness still collects and, when live credentials plus `acli` are absent, skips for that reason; its well-formed plan contract cites the canonical plan-entry owner rather than `reconcile._build_plan_entries`.\n- [ ] Mode ordering comparisons retain all current ordering semantics without `rank()`.\n- [ ] Focused inbound/orchestration/mode tests, raw shim-consumer scans, lint, typecheck, and the ticket verify command set pass."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788576827444796001,"uuid":"d4777932-8733-490b-aa27-9aeeba3d8e2f"}